        "original_id": "0457c670-4e6d-5548-8456-d3aef95c3e87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Cocky, Picture\n- People: Kid Rock, Sheryl Crow, Allison Moorer\n- Companies: Atlantic, Crow's label\n- Concepts: duet recordings, single release rights, radio re-recording\n\nFacts:\n- The album Cocky is known for featuring the ballad \"Picture\" as a duet recording by Kid Rock and Sheryl Crow.\n- Atlantic was initially unable to obtain release rights from Sheryl Crow's label to issue the album version of \"Picture\" as a single.\n- Kid Rock re-recorded \"Picture\" for radio with Allison Moorer as an alternative version because the Sheryl Crow duet could not initially be released as a single.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3ff747a8-ec8d-51f7-9089-e8479ea49004",
        "text": "Page: Cocky (album). Sentence: The album is known for featuring the ballad \"Picture\", recorded as a duet with Sheryl Crow.\nPage: Picture (song). Sentence: Rock re-recorded the song for the radio with alternative country singer Allison Moorer because Atlantic was initially unable to get the rights from Crow's label to release the album version as a single.",
